 as nick the cable guy he chased  kramer through the streets of new york  city and later hugged it out with him  after apologizing on behalf of plaza  cable for making him wait at home all  day  new jersey native and best known for his  turn as bartender jacques renault in  twin peaks twin peaks fire walk with me  and later as jacques cousin in twin  peaks the return ulkowitz retired from  acting following several knee surgeries  and later died of complications from  infections in 2021 at the age of 72. his  son screenwriter zack okowitz said in a  statement he was a good man who pushed  his love for creativity and the arts  into everything he did  over the span of 27 episodes of seinfeld  viewers got a chance to see just why  george costanza was the way he was it  was all because of a comically fraught  relationship with his overbearing  overprotective judgmental and often  shrieking mother estelle costanza  you're wearing that shirt  you've had it for five years already why  don't you buy a new shirt  estelle was often a hindrance to  george's goals or a burden to be dealt  with she was great at embarrassing her  son as was the case in her first  appearance in the episode the contest i  go out for a quart of milk i come home  and find my son treating his body like  it was an amusement park  before her signature role of estelle  costanza on seinfeld estelle harris had  a few dozen parts she only began  seriously acting in her late 40s with  frequent theatrical and tv commercial  roles according to cnn after seinfeld  she often played a version of estelle  costanza through voice work most notably  as mrs potato head in the toy story  movies  harris died in april 2022 at the age of  93.  veteran actor philip bakerhall appeared  on screen nearly 200 times in a 50-year  career that stretched from the early  1970s to the 2020s a definitive  character actor he was always noticeable  for his uniquely raspy voice and intense  stare which he brought to dozens of  shows and movies paul was a member of  writer director paul thomas anderson's  repertory players landing major parts in  hard 8 boogie nights and magnolia he was  also part of the award-winning ensemble  of the contender argo and dogville  regardless he is probably best  remembered for the character he played  on one episode of seinfeld which he  reprised in the series finale he  portrayed the wonderfully and aptly  named lieutenant joe bookman the stern  and relentless library cop who tracks  down jerry over a book that was 20 years  overdue  paul died at home in glendale california  in june 2022 he was 90 years old  there isn't anyone on seinfeld who loved  adored and cherished the heart to love  jerry seinfeld more than his mother  helen seinfeld how could anyone not like  you  she visits jerry often at his home in  new york city when he can't make it down  to florida to see her and her husband  morty those visits usually morph into  meddling and budding in verging on  smothering the doting relentlessly sunny  and persuasive helen appeared in 21  seinfeld episodes over the course of the  series playing the nosy helen  immediately after a recurring role as  the nosy neighbor in alf was liz  sheridan a veteran of multiple 70s  broadway productions and many 80s  sitcoms  her representative told deadline that  she died in her sleep in april 2022 she  was 93.  catherine cates portrayed an unnamed but  plot pivotal character in two episodes  of seinfeld that aired two years apart  jerry and delane head to the royal  bakery to purchase a chocolate bobcat  but are unable to because they didn't  take a number when they arrived enabling  someone else to buy the last one they  purchase a lesser cinnamon bobka and  must deal with the busy harried  counterwoman to return it kate pops up  again as the bakery cashier in the 1996  episode the rye once more trying to buy  something at the royal bakery only to  have someone else purchase it right  before he can jerry loses out on a  marble ride to mabel choate which he  infamously gets after mugging her and  taking it a prolific character actor who  appeared in law and order svu and  oranges the new black kates died in  florida in january 2022 after a history  of lung cancer she was 73.  in the episode the breasts jerry and  elaine are asked by some friends to be  the god parents of their new baby in  accordance with that the pair must find  a moil the jewish holy figure who  performs the sacred rite of circumcision  unfortunately the guy they've hired  isn't exactly the best he's prone to  wild mood swings and may have even once  faced malpractice allegations for  botching another breast it all boils  over into a full-on fight between jerry  and the moyle portraying the unnamed but  memorable moyle was character actor  charles levin who apart from seinfeld  was probably best known for the pilot  episode of the golden girls and multiple  woody allen films in july 2019 his  remains were found in a remote area of  oregon where he had gotten lost and  stranded he was 70.  [Music]
 

